Returns a heatmap of how often each pair of interpreters used the same \code{target} for the same \code{source} unit, for a single round of elicitation. Each tile shows the number of \code{source} units where both interpreters of a pair assigned membership to a \code{target}, with a colour gradient from light to dark teal for more source units. Empty tiles mean the pair never used that target for the same source unit. Rows with missing or zero membership are not counted as use. The plot helps to spot targets that pairs of interpreters agree or disagree on.
